2026-10-09T17:56:09.7952308Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8028614Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8036368Z [0m
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8036836Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8037245Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8037366Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8037743Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8038023Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8038170Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8038309Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8038527Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8038624Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8038865Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8039167Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8039420Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8039613Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8039701Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8039828Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8039963Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8040106Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8040309Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8040382Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8040447Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8040533Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8041066Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8041443Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8049293Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8049441Z I will:
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8049558Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8049759Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8050141Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8050777Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8051112Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8051329Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8051490Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8051726Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8051927Z    /root
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8062962Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8063391Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8072212Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8072645Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8072792Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8074040Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8074664Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8089456Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8089970Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8097967Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8098442Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8098687Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8098795Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8098897Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8099020Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8099165Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8099468Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8099639Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8099734Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8099972Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8100121Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8100291Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8100612Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8100743Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8100752Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8100994Z [32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8107768Z [0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8144350Z been installed on this system.
2026-10-09T17:56:09.8144712Z 
